<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/3/eng@/~part_II__cl_4__subsec_3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://docs.oasis-open.org/legaldocml/ns/akn/3.0#subsection> <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/3/eng@> .
<https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/3/eng@/~part_II__cl_4__subsec_3> <https://schema.org/text> "Where, after considering the report from the Director General, the Minister is satisfied that the contraventions were, or the apprehended contraventions ABATTOIRS (PRIVATISATION) are, of a serious nature or has affected or is likely to affect public interest or safety and that the licensed operator has refused to take or has not taken all such steps as appear necessary to the Minister for the purpose of securing compliance with the condition in question, the Minister may give to the licensed operator notice stating that he proposes to suspend or revoke, as the case may be, its licence and such notice shall also set out—"@en <https://cheeleong.dev/data-parlimen/akn/my/bill/dr/1993/3/eng@> .
